<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Forli</h1><p class="st-meta">1315 CE – 1480 CE (approx.) · capital Forli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ordelaffi lordship of Forlì in Romagna, a Ghibelline house that hosted Dante and long defied papal armies.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ordelaffi family led Forlì's Ghibellines, and in 1315 they became lords of the city. They ruled, sometimes as papal vicars and sometimes in open rebellion, over Forlì and at times <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesena">Cesena</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> towns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scarpetta-ordelaffi">Scarpetta Ordelaffi</a> hosted the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> around 1303. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-ii-ordelaffi">Francesco II Ordelaffi</a> resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gil-alvarez-carrillo-de-albornoz">Cardinal Albornoz's</a> campaign to restore papal rule for years; his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cia-degli-ubaldini">Cia degli Ubaldini</a> defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesena">Cesena</a> in 1357 until forced to surrender, and Forlì fell in 1359. The family regained the city in 1376. Forlì lived from farming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> plain and from the condottiere careers of its lords.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pino-iii-ordelaffi">Pino III Ordelaffi</a> died in 1480, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-iv">Pope Sixtus IV</a> granted Forlì to his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girolamo-riario">Girolamo Riario</a>, joining it to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-imola-and-forli">Lordship of Imola and Forli</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1315 CE – 1480 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.87%;width:3.28%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1315 CE – 1480 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Forli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Scarpetta Ordelaffi, Francesco II Ordelaffi, Pino III Ordelaffi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Romagnol, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ordelaffi lordship, Forli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1398&amp;focus=lordship-of-forli" aria-label="Lordship of Forli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4929 603 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Forli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5249 859h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5249 859h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Italy. <a href="/atlas?year=1398&amp;focus=lordship-of-forli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
